Zink: do not read missing dma-buf fence semaphores.

Flushing a batch that used a dma-buf creates one exportable SYNC_FD semaphore
per plane and appends those that succeed; submit_queue() then reads one per
plane unconditionally. PanVK's kbase backend cannot create SYNC_FD
semaphores, so the array is empty and its data pointer NULL: Firefox
crashed in the flush thread on its first imported VA-API frame. Attach
fences only for the semaphores that exist; without them the dma-buf keeps
the synchronous behaviour it has when implicit sync is unavailable.

--- a/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_batch.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_batch.c
@@ -820,6 +820,8 @@
 
    unsigned i = 0;
    VkSemaphore *sem = bs->signal_semaphores.data;
+   /* one semaphore per plane, unless the driver could not create them */
+   unsigned num_sem = util_dynarray_num_elements(&bs->signal_semaphores, VkSemaphore);
    hash_table_foreach(&bs->dmabuf_exports, entry) {
       struct zink_resource *res = (void*)entry->key;
       /* Add the batch's fence as a write fence if the batch wrote the image,
@@ -827,7 +829,7 @@
        */
       if (res->obj->exportable_dmabuf) {
          bool write = entry->data != NULL;
-         for (; res; res = zink_resource(res->base.b.next))
+         for (; res && i < num_sem; res = zink_resource(res->base.b.next))
             zink_screen_import_dmabuf_semaphore(screen, res, sem[i++], write);
       }
 
